      "message": "fix(app): every op that reads the setup's stock digests it in its stamp\n\nThe rapid-in-stock laws (#96, #106), the prior acquittal, the reach and\nR-plane laws and the lathe meridian bar all read the setup's stock, but\nonly Drill's stamp digested it (#77/#91). Enlarging the stock after\ngeneration left a Contour whose dive now lands in material reading Ok,\nand the post let it through.\n\nThe stock reaches every generator through one seam (collect_job hands\nevery non-stock-sourced kind the stock's facets and box), so the set is\nexplicit: every op whose source is not the stock itself\n(operation::reads_setup_stock). Its stamp now carries the stock term:\npresence, placement, the mesh signature, and the shape's kind and\nparameters. The stock-as-source arm moves to the new stamp_stock module\nwith its bytes unchanged, keeping stamp.rs under 400 lines.\n\nExisting saved projects read their part-sourced ops Stale once and clear\non regenerate (the same one-time churn as earlier stamp moves).\n\nPinned by stock_stamp: enlarging the stock over a contour's dive stales\nit and blocks the post; moving the stock stales it; undo returns Ok; a\nwork-material change stales nothing.\n\nFixes #156\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
